{"B_expression":"-1/(2*(1+sqrt(1+r))**2)","C_expression":"-1/2","derivation":"Retain the inherited program unchanged. The feedback confirms the construction operates as designed: (1) B(r) = -1/(2(1+sqrt(1+r))^2) gives exact cancellation of the pure remainder when u=0 (residuals at ~1e-71, machine epsilon at 70 digits), verified by the identity_defect column. The algebraic identity g = r/2 + r^2*B(r) = sqrt(1+r)-1 yields z_new = sqrt(1+r) so z_new^2 = 1+r = p exactly. (2) C = -1/2 cancels the leading O(ur) cross term in E = pure + cross. Numerical confirmation: for UNIFORM rows with u≈±0.0078 and r≈±0.0002, pure≈∓1.5e-6 and cross≈±1.5e-6 nearly cancel, leaving residual≈±1e-8 (O(ur^2)+O(u^2 r) remainder). (3) Rows with |u|>1/4 (e.g., LEFT x=1/8 s=0 with u=-0.5) fall outside chi_u support and correctly receive only g=r/2 with large residual, as designed. Both bodies are C-infinity on an open neighborhood of the closed rectangle: B is rational in sqrt(1+r) with 1+r>0 for r>-1 (encompassing the r-rectangle [-1/2,1/2]), and C is a constant. The certificate confirms ANALYTIC_ON_CORE_NEIGHBORHOOD for both. No modification is warranted: the local algebraic cancellation is optimal at its target order, and higher-order terms (O(ur^2), O(u^2 r), O(r^3)) would require state-dependent or multi-term corrections that add complexity without addressing the stated purpose of the coefficient-field operator.","inspect":[{"file_id":"CALC/draft.json","limit":4096,"offset":0}],"note":"Retained. The two-slot covariance quotient operator with source-exact B and constant C=-1/2 is stable and performing at its designed order. Successor observations: (a) For the next target (p1 = p0 + tau^2*k1), rows with small nonzero u will show residuals of order O(u*r^2) + O(u^2*r), roughly 1e-8 to 1e-7 for the current parameter regime (tau=1/128, h=1/200). This is the expected floor for this construction and does not indicate failure. (b) The chi_u transition band (|u| in [1/8, 1/4]) will partially engage the C=-1/2 correction; monitor for any numerical stiffness there. (c) The large-amplitude rows (LEFT/RIGHT/BOTH with |z| up to 33) are permanently outside the chi_r support and will always show the uncorrected linear residual; their status is structurally NO_APPLIED or APPLIED-with-linear-g, not a program defect. (d) The analytic certificate is CONDITIONAL_SMOOTH_FAMILY, sufficient for the local coefficient construction but not a full PDE or NS theorem certificate."}